labels: order 1 | order 2 | order 3 | order 4 | order 5
answer: yes | yes | no | no | no
wrong[yes | no | no | no | no]: B and C don't depend on each other, so either can come second.
wrong[yes | yes | no | yes | no]: In order 4, D comes before C, but the edge C → D needs C first.
