          "cook": ["serve"], "table": ["serve"], "serve": []}
print(rounds(dinner))
```
hint: Each round collects all the free jobs first, and only then marks them as done.
hint: `done.update(ready)` adds every job in the list to the set.
right: Jobs found free in the same round don't depend on each other, so they can run together. The number of rounds is the length of the longest chain of dependencies, here buy, chop, cook, serve.
